description: Next.js + Tailwind perf & cost rules
globs: app/**/*.tsx, components/**/*.tsx, next.config.* , tailwind.config.*,alwaysApply: false
---

## Rendering
- Prefer **static** or **ISR** where possible; use **Server Components** by default.
- Only opt into SSR for truly dynamic paths. Push heavy logic to the server/edge.

## Bundles & Network
- Use **dynamic import** for heavy client components; no global client state unless required.
- Use Next Image and font optimization; set proper caching headers; avoid unbounded rewrites.
- Keep Tailwind production build lean (proper `content` globs; purge unused classes).

## Runtime & Infra
- Avoid unnecessary edge functions (cost); when used, keep payloads tiny.
- Memoize pure client components; avoid re-renders; use React Server Actions carefully.

## Diagnostics
- Add basic web-vitals logging and measure TTFB/LCP/CLS on previews before merge.